---
import Policy from "../layouts/Policy.astro";
---

<Policy title="Terms">
  <h2>Who runs the fund</h2>
  <p>
    The&nbsp;Rupee&nbsp;Fund is a FOSS United community initiative run by community members. The <a
      href="/people"
      class="inline-link">community team</a
    > runs this website. Adoption of Foundation policies does not give the Foundation control of the fund.
  </p>
  <h2>Policies we adopt</h2>
  <p>
    We adopt the standards for lawful use and respect for intellectual property in the{" "}
    <a
      href="https://fossunited.org/terms-of-service"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      class="inline-link">FOSS United terms of service</a
    >, as reviewed on 7 September 2026. The terms on this page apply to rupeefund.org. References in
    the source to Foundation services, ownership, contacts, or agreements do not assign those roles
    to the Foundation for this fund. We do not adopt the source provision that makes submissions
    Foundation property. Our <a href="/privacy" class="inline-link">Privacy</a>{" "}
    page states how we use form submissions. Where the source differs from our local terms, our local
    terms apply. Later changes to the source do not change these terms automatically.
  </p>
  <h2>Before launch</h2>
  <p>
    This site collects requests for a launch email and answers that help us plan the fund. Signing
    up creates no payment obligation, membership, voting right, or promise of a grant. We take no
    payments through this site at this stage. Proposed contribution amounts and funding plans can
    change before launch.
  </p>
  <h2>Use of this site</h2>
  <p>
    Use this site lawfully. Do not submit unlawful content, misuse another person’s email address,
    or interfere with the site. Respect the rights and licences of content owners. A link to another
    organisation does not make that organisation an operator of this fund.
  </p>
  <h2>Before contributions open</h2>
  <p>
    We will publish the payment recipient, payment terms, cancellation process, and refund
    responsibilities before we accept contributions. These terms do not promise a tax benefit or
    identify the Foundation as the recipient of future payments.
  </p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will publish changes here with a new effective date. The local{" "}
    <a href="/privacy" class="inline-link">Privacy</a>,{" "}
    <a href="/refunds" class="inline-link">Refunds</a>, and{" "}
    <a href="/code-of-conduct" class="inline-link">Code of conduct</a> pages add rules for those subjects.
  </p>
</Policy>
